<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_Miasma_CrecheScatterer.xml   UtinniPatches - MIASMA_MECHANICS_1 M6 build pass

  Declares the GenStepDef for RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces (the shared,
  already-built set-piece scatterer, RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards),
  configured per miasma_kit_spec.md M6: N sites (INVENTED 2-4 per map) on
  brine-side shallow water, each spawning a RUT_CrecheMarker + one anchored
  warden pawn. Registration onto Base_Player is the separate Patches/
  RUT_Miasma_CrecheScatterer_Register.xml file, same split this folder's
  own RUT_Miasma_GradientAxisGenStep.xml/Patches/RUT_Miasma_GradientAxis_
  Register.xml pair already established for M1.

  order 235: strictly after RUT_GenStep_GradientAxis (225) — the spec's own
  words, "validator reads M1's axis — strict ordering after
  RM_GenStep_GradientAxis" — with headroom before the 320+ range this
  folder's other scatter GenSteps already occupy.

  countPer10kCellsRange 0.4~0.6 is this repo's own already-established
  reading of "2-4 per map": RUT_ScaldWreckScatter.xml (SCALD_MECHANICS_1,
  same folder) uses the identical 0.4~0.6 range for its own "a few per
  map" set pieces — for a 250-cell-side map, GenStep_Scatterer.
  CountFromPer10kCells resolves that to ~2.5-3.75 sites, i.e. 2-4 after
  rounding. Reused rather than re-derived.

  validators: RM_ScattererValidator_BrineShallowWater (this pass's own new
  class) reads RM_MapComponent_GradientAxis (M1) directly — the strict
  ordering above is what makes that axis already-painted when this GenStep
  runs. warnOnFail false: this GenStepDef is registered globally onto
  Base_Player (below), and the validator legitimately rejects every cell on
  every non-Miasma map (no RM_GradientAxisExtension on that map's biome) —
  without this, every OTHER biome's map-gen would log a spurious "could not
  find cell to generate at" warning.

  elements: RM_SetPieceElement_SpawnMarker places RUT_CrecheMarker first,
  then RM_SetPieceElement_AnchoredPawn spawns the warden pawn and anchors it
  to that same marker (anchorMarkerDef, found by def at the shared site
  cell — see that class's own header for why this ordering matters).

  pawnKind RSW_OpeeSeaKiller (mandrake.rsw.swbestiary) is a WIRING
  PLACEHOLDER — see the pawnKind element's own inline comment. Full
  reasoning: infrastructure/state/items/MIASMA_MECHANICS_1.md's M6 build
  pass section.

  MayRequire is load-bearing on the GenStepDef itself (not per-<li>): every
  referenced Class/def in this file lives in mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards
  or mandrake.rsw.swbestiary, so the whole def is gated on both being
  active, same posture as this folder's own RUT_MoatFusePost.xml precedent
  ("gating the entire def is correct... this def's only content is the
  comp itself").
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards,mandrake.rsw.swbestiary">
    <defName>RUT_GenStep_CrecheScatterer</defName>
    <order>235</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_GenStep_PlacedSetPieces">
      <countPer10kCellsRange>0.4~0.6</countPer10kCellsRange>
      <spotMustBeStandable>true</spotMustBeStandable>
      <warnOnFail>false</warnOnFail>
      <validators>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_ScattererValidator_BrineShallowWater">
          <minSalinity>0.6</minSalinity>
        </li>
      </validators>
      <elements>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_SetPieceElement_SpawnMarker">
          <markerDef>RUT_CrecheMarker</markerDef>
        </li>
        <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_SetPieceElement_AnchoredPawn">
          <!-- PLACEHOLDER - roster pass replaces with the real warden-mother
               kind. sea_beasts_roster.md's nursery/adult pairing owns this
               content (miasma_kit_spec.md M6's own scope line: "The
               warden/juvenile PawnKindDefs are roster content ... this kit
               ships the scatterer and the marker"). RSW_OpeeSeaKiller
               chosen as the WIRING placeholder because it is thematically
               closest among everything already shipped: an ambush sea
               predator whose own juvenile (RSW_OpeeSeaKillerJuv,
               SeaBeasts_NurseryJuveniles.xml) is already described as
               lingering "at the crèche mouths where it hatched" — the
               crèche framing already exists on this exact species pair,
               it is simply the wrong scale/species for a "warden mother." -->
          <pawnKind>RSW_OpeeSeaKiller</pawnKind>
          <anchorMarkerDef>RUT_CrecheMarker</anchorMarkerDef>
        </li>
      </elements>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
